import{_ as i,o as t,c as o,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 269 | Tang-Luo Decomposition | Historical Regression Simulation: Civilization Trajectory When Tang Luo Secludes Himself for a Hundred Years","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 269 | Tang-Luo Decomposition | Historical Regression Simulation: Civilization Trajectory When Tang Luo Secludes Himself for a Hundred Years","no":269,"module":2,"tags":["Tang-Luo","Historical Regression","Hundred-Year Seclusion","Civilization Trajectory","Myriad-Realms Benchmark"],"related":["71-Pre-Anchor Era","30-Five Symbiotic Civilization Typology Overview","29-Symbiosis Degree Evaluation System"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0269_模块2-唐罗-历史倒退模拟.md","filePath":"en/0269_模块2-唐罗-历史倒退模拟.md"}'),s={name:"en/0269_模块2-唐罗-历史倒退模拟.md"};function a(r,e,l,u,d,c){return t(),o("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n('<h1 id="entry-269-tang-luo-decomposition-historical-regression-simulation-civilization-trajectory-when-tang-luo-secludes-himself-for-a-hundred-years" tabindex="-1">Entry 269 | Tang-Luo Decomposition | Historical Regression Simulation: Civilization Trajectory When Tang Luo Secludes Himself for a Hundred Years <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-269-tang-luo-decomposition-historical-regression-simulation-civilization-trajectory-when-tang-luo-secludes-himself-for-a-hundred-years" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 269 | Tang-Luo Decomposition | Historical Regression Simulation: Civilization Trajectory When Tang Luo Secludes Himself for a Hundred Years&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Full Decomposition of the Tang-Luo System (Entry 19)</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-remove-tang-luo-from-the-board-how-does-civilization-walk" tabindex="-1">Introduction: Remove Tang Luo from the board, how does civilization walk <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-remove-tang-luo-from-the-board-how-does-civilization-walk" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: Remove Tang Luo from the board, how does civilization walk&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Among the six top-level axioms, the causal self-discipline axiom requires observing first then limitedly interfering; the collective ascension axiom requires no single-point dependency. This entry conducts the most critical thought experiment in the Quest Sediment Domain: Tang Luo secludes himself for a hundred years, does not ask worldly affairs, where will the civilization he established go? This entry takes the law-first axiom as core. Protagonist uniqueness dependency judgment: <strong>Tang Luo = high dependency / bestowal-style civilization</strong> — this entry is precisely this judgment&#39;s scenario deduction. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s evaluation base has been upgraded to six top-level axioms.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The hundred-year seclusion simulation&#39;s essence is removing &quot;Tang Luo in-office-period energy&quot; from civilization, watching the naked-running civilization. Waste&#39;s form becomes visible here:</p><ul><li><strong>No one backfills</strong>: Tang Luo leaves, adjudication, transmission, distribution, supervision all idling. These posts should have been shared by institutions, now can only be held by him alone — the price of combined holding is, once he leaves, all posts simultaneously go unemployed</li><li><strong>Transmission vacuum</strong>: high-tier Great Dao has no one to explain it, new disciples receiving fragmentary chapters have no one to Q&amp;A. Knowledge stock starts naturally decaying</li><li><strong>Credit contraction</strong>: Tang Luo is gone, all &quot;graces,&quot; &quot;privileges,&quot; &quot;appointments&quot; he issued start depreciating. Social credit system goes into seclusion chamber with him</li></ul><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression-hundred-year-timeline" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression: Hundred-Year Timeline <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression-hundred-year-timeline" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression: Hundred-Year Timeline&quot;">​</a></h2><p>By Quest Sediment Domain simulation, Tang Luo&#39;s hundred-year seclusion civilization trajectory has four segments:</p><p><strong>Years 0–10: Inertia period</strong></p><ul><li>Old institutions still running, academy as usual, resources as usual</li><li>Surface prosperity, but every key decision is delayed by &quot;waiting for Tang Luo to leave seclusion&quot;</li><li>Old aristocratic family remnants begin tentative activity</li></ul><p><strong>Years 10–30: Crack period</strong></p><ul><li>Academy has personnel strife, who will succeed as principal?</li><li>High-tier methods have no one to explain, demonic-deviation rate rises</li><li>Border foreign races start probing, border generals dare not decide, retreating step by step</li><li>The first batch of ballads &quot;missing Tang Luo&quot; appear — missing itself is a crisis signal</li></ul><p><strong>Years 30–70: Restoration period</strong></p><ul><li>Old aristocratic families change skins and return, new powerholders self-claim &quot;Tang Luo&#39;s old subordinates&quot; and re-monopolize</li><li>Academy changes from &quot;universal benefit&quot; back to &quot;aristocratic prep school&quot;</li><li>Mid-low tier methods nominally still there, actually new powerholders set various hidden thresholds</li><li>Human-demon border war breaks out, because no one leads reconciliation</li></ul><p><strong>Years 70–100: Regression complete</strong></p><ul><li>Civilization on the surface still &quot;misses Tang Luo,&quot; actually has returned to his pre-reform state</li><li>If Tang Luo leaves seclusion at this point, he will find his hundred years of effort have left only a few place names</li></ul><p>Conclusion: <strong>hundred-year seclusion = hundred-year civilizational regression.</strong> Not dramatic collapse, but slow-boiled frog restoration.</p><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Predatory thinking exposed by the hundred-year simulation:</p><ul><li><strong>Single-point dependency is predation</strong>: betting civilization&#39;s fate on one person deprives civilization of the ability to bear things itself. The hundred-year simulation proves this deprivation&#39;s price is an entire era</li><li><strong>Legacy-favor illusion</strong>: Tang Luo thought the institutions he left were protecting civilization, actually the institutions were only his shadow. The shadow rapidly dissipates after he leaves the wall</li><li><strong>Good will undefended</strong>: he never prepared for &quot;when I am not here.&quot; This is not negligence, but the bestowal system&#39;s intrinsic feature — bestowers do not intend for all beings to stand on their own</li></ul><p>By the Gu Chensha / Tang Luo judgment table standard: Tang Luo = <strong>enlightened predator</strong>, the hundred-year simulation gives his &quot;predation&quot; temporal dimension: every day he is not there, predation automatically executes.</p><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Tang-Luo Hundred-Year Seclusion</th><th>Anchor Republican Hundred Years</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Posts idle</td><td>Anchor Council legislates as usual, Executive Committee administers as usual</td></tr><tr><td>Knowledge decays</td><td>Alaya Network saves all knowledge, no one decays</td></tr><tr><td>Credit contracts</td><td>Law-anchored authority benefits all beings, credit rests on law</td></tr><tr><td>Old forces restore</td><td>Anti-monopoly law, Myriad Races Republican Constitution rigid clauses, restoration is unconstitutional</td></tr><tr><td>Hundred-year regression</td><td>Hundred years running as usual, even faster without single-point ties</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Alternative&#39;s crux: Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s civilization does not even have the concept of &quot;seclusion&quot; — because no one can &quot;represent&quot; the entire civilization to seclude.</p><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: replicate Tang-Luo civilization, marking its post-combined-holding map</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: inject &quot;Tang Luo hundred-year seclusion&quot; event</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: record institutional operation rate, knowledge stock, social credit in four segments</li><li><strong>Review conclusion</strong>: output &quot;Tang Luo Hundred-Year Seclusion Report&quot; — hundred-year post regression rate about 80%, i.e., Tang Luo&#39;s reform results retained under 20%</li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Setting self-consistency: medium-high</strong>. Scenario deduction is self-consistent with Tang-Luo system&#39;s internal logic</li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk: medium</strong>. If the author does not want to write this &quot;seclusion means regression,&quot; can only make Tang Luo never seclude — this itself is retcon (using setting cheats to solve institutional absence)</li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency</strong>: high. The hundred-year simulation is the strongest evidence for the &quot;high dependency&quot; judgment</li></ul><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: Tang Luo leaves, civilization&#39;s deployable energy drops 80%</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: single-point dependency = depriving civilization of self-reliance</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: after a hundred years Tang Luo&#39;s effort remains 20%, proving institutions matter more than people</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: during seclusion Myriad Races&#39; situation deteriorates first</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: cross-plane civilization cannot withstand any single-point seclusion</li><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power is inherent in all; the easygoing retain a guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin erases predatory motivation, predatory involution loses meaning from the root</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Tang-Luo hundred-year seclusion simulation is the cruelest proof of the &quot;high dependency&quot; judgment. Heng Yuan Zhou does not deny Tang Luo&#39;s greatness, only says: if a civilization needs Tang Luo to never be able to seclude, then this civilization has not grown up yet. True adulthood is allowing anyone to seclude, civilization runs as usual.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./71-前锚点时代.html">71-Pre-Anchor Era</a> · <a href="./30-五种共生文明分型总览.html">30-Five Symbiotic Civilization Typology Overview</a> · <a href="./29-共生度评估体系.html">29-Symbiosis Degree Evaluation System</a></li></ul>',36)])])}const m=i(s,[["render",a]]);export{g as __pageData,m as default};
